\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Delete ordering\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 A delete with a newer timestamp creates a tombstone.\
An older delete cannot replace that newer version.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Tombstone vs. old write\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 After deletion, an old write remains rejected.\
A sufficiently newer write can replace the tombstone.\
This verifies that deletes participate in version ordering rather than behaving as a separate mechanism.\
