\f3\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 22. Delete coordinator logic\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Delete follows the same replication/quorum architecture as Put, but instead of sending a value it sends:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f5\fs26 \cf0 key + deletion timestamp\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs24 \cf0 to the replicas.\
The replicas create tombstones locally.\
The coordinator counts acknowledgements and compares them with the write quorum.\
The internal 
\f5\fs26 ReplicateDelete
\f2\fs24  RPC therefore has the same passive role as 
\f5\fs26 ReplicatePut
\f2\fs24 : apply the requested version locally and acknowledge processing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 One implementation detail worth remembering:
\f2\b0  your current final 
\f5\fs26 Delete
\f2\fs24  has a special local-replica branch that immediately returns after the local delete, rather than continuing to collect a quorum. So while the intended Phase 3 design is quorum-based deletion, the current final implementation does not actually perform the same complete quorum calculation when the coordinator itself is a replica. This is a difference between the intended design and the exact code you finished with, and is worth carrying forward rather than forgetting it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 23. gRPC deadlines and failure handling\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Remote replication calls use 
\f5\fs26 grpc::ClientContext
\f2\fs24  with a deadline.\
The purpose is critical:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 A coordinator must not wait forever for a dead/unreachable replica.\
If a replica does not respond before the deadline, the RPC fails and the coordinator can treat that replica as unavailable while determining whether quorum is still achievable.\
You learned that timeout behavior is essential for fault tolerance: without deadlines, a crashed server could cause a coordinator RPC to hang indefinitely.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf0 Another implementation detail:
\f2\b0  in your final code, 
\f5\fs26 SendReplicatePut
\f2\fs24  and 
\f5\fs26 SendReplicateGet
\f2\fs24  use a 2000 ms deadline, but 
\f5\fs26 SendReplicateDelete
\f2\fs24  currently uses 
\f3\b 2000 microseconds = 2 milliseconds
\f2\b0 , not 2000 milliseconds = 2 seconds. That is a likely accidental unit mismatch in the final code and should be remembered when you start Phase 4/debugging.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

