\f3\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 31. Graceful server shutdown\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 You also retained the signal-handling mechanism.\
The server uses an atomic shutdown flag.\
When the process receives 
\f5\fs26 SIGINT
\f2\fs24  or 
\f5\fs26 SIGTERM
\f2\fs24 , the signal handler sets that flag.\
The server's main loop notices it and then:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls32\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 requests gRPC shutdown,\
\ls32\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 waits for the server to finish,\
\ls32\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 exits cleanly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
