\f3\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 34. Important distributed-systems concepts you learned\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The bigger learning from Phase 3 is not just the code.\
You now have practical exposure to:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Replication\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Keeping multiple copies of the same data on different machines/nodes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Preference lists\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Deterministically selecting the replicas for a key from the consistent-hash ring.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Coordinator\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 The node that receives a request and coordinates the operation among replicas.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Quorum\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Requiring only a subset of replicas to acknowledge an operation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Read/write quorum intersection\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Understanding why 
\f5\fs26 R + W > N
\f2\fs24  matters.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Fault tolerance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Understanding that one failed replica can be tolerated with 
\f5\fs26 N=3, R=2, W=2
\f2\fs24 , while two failures exceed the available quorum.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Versioning\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Attaching metadata to values so different versions can be compared.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Last-Write-Wins\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Choosing the version with the highest timestamp.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Tombstones\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Representing deletion as a versioned state rather than physically removing the key.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Eventual inconsistency between replicas\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Understanding that replicas can temporarily disagree and that the coordinator resolves conflicting versions using version metadata.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Failure detection through deadlines\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Understanding that an unavailable remote node must eventually be treated as unavailable rather than waiting forever.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f3\b\fs28 \cf0 Passive replication handlers\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Separating the coordinator's responsibility from a replica's responsibility.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
